# The working tree is LF, on every machine.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks files out as CRLF (`core.autocrlf=true`)
# while `.editorconfig` and `.prettierrc` both say LF — so the formatter wants
# to rewrite every line of half the repo, and the other half, written by tools
# that do not go through git, is already LF. That is the mixed tree this fixes.
# `eol=lf` wins over whatever `core.autocrlf` is set to locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: a byte is a byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.jsc binary
*.tgz binary
*.pem binary
